{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5993,
  "title": "Fluent: style Web Chat elements through the CSS module theme",
  "body": "> Fluent styles Web Chat elements by their readable class names (`:global(.bubble)`), so Web Chat cannot drop or rename them.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\nNone: internal refactoring with no visible change, label `no-changelog`.\n\n## Description\n\nFluent's CSS modules selected 101 class names of Web Chat CSS modules through `:global()`. Fluent's rules for Web Chat elements now live in one override CSS module, which `FluentThemeProvider` passes whole through `<CSSModuleThemeComposer>` (#5984). Each element gets at most two Fluent classes.\n\n## Design\n\n- `fluent-theme/src/private/fluentCSSModuleTheme.module.css`: rules moved unchanged from Fluent's `PartGroupingDecorator`, `SendBox` and `Theme` modules, keeping order, regions and scope, so the cascade does not change\n- A rule without styles keeps its class with `--webchat-preserve-reason: target-class;`, which `esbuildPlugins.mjs` strips after the class map is built; vibe-grep fails the build if one is left\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `FluentThemeProvider`: wraps everything in `<CSSModuleThemeComposer>`\n- `ActivityButton`, `SendBox`: classes for themes, kept by the declaration above\n- `fluentCSSModuleTheme.spec.ts`: only the override module uses Web Chat local names, never through `:global()`\n- root `package.json`: `lightningcss` dev dependency (1.32.0, as installed today)\n- No snapshot changes in the Fluent html2 tests\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
